[x] 59 Bridge Quote node (PnBridgeQuote) -- monitor real swap rates on crypto
       bridges. The FX Converter (PnRate) reports a CoinGecko mid-market price;
       that says nothing about what a swap actually pays out, where a 1-3%
       spread, a flat network fee and per-pair min/max limits all bite. This
       node asks a real bridge for a quote on a concrete amount and emits it
       every tick. A PnHttp subclass in core with a -gui companion, mirroring
       PnRate; no PnNodeClass vfunc added, so no plugin ABI bump. Two providers
       in v1, selected by a `bridge` enum so two nodes can compare the same pair
       side by side on one graph. Currencies reuse PN_TYPE_CURRENCY, so the
       dialog gets the FX Converter's icon+ticker picker for free; a pair the
       selected provider does not list marks the node unconfigured rather than
       failing at fetch time.
       [x] 59.1 PulseLN back-end. One keyless GET to api.pulseln.com/c/prices
             returns the whole cross-rate matrix; there is no per-amount quote
             endpoint, so pulseln_parse() reproduces the swap page's own
             formula (cross-rate, minus the flat network fee, minus the DLN
             fee for the assets in DLN_LIST, minus the PF[FROMTO]/F
             percentage), and gates on STATUS[from] and PS[to] both being
             "online". The site scales the network term by
             grn(DIFF) = |random()*DIFF - 100| / 100, which is 0.9999..1.0 --
             cosmetic jitter, so the C code uses 1.0 and stays deterministic.
             UNDOCUMENTED, UNVERSIONED endpoint: it can change or be locked
             without notice, and a shape change must surface as a readable
             status, never a crash.
       [x] 59.2 ChangeNOW back-end. v1 only: /exchange-amount quotes directly
             and /exchange-range supplies the limits in a second request
             issued from emit_message. v1 needs no API key; v2's
             estimated-amount answers 401 without one, and a v2 key is granted
             only on request. If a key is ever wanted it belongs in a
             host-provisioned profile (PnProfileSchema + PnVault,
             PN_FIELD_SECRET), never in a node property.
       [x] 59.3 Source shape, unlike PnRate. No input port; emits one message
             per tick. The trigger override still emits when the freshness gate
             skips the fetch -- staying silent (as PnRate does) would leave a
             reopened worksheet's displays blank. Failures emit too, with
             success=FALSE and a human-readable output. quote/rate/fee/limits
             and last-update persist with the worksheet, so a reopened flow
             repaints from cache without touching the provider.
       [x] 59.4 Registration + build: lib/Makefile.am (4 lists),
             pn-node-factory.c, pn-gui.c, data/Makefile.am (help page),
             tests/unit/Makefile.am. Also registered examples/crypto/ in
             examples/Makefile.am -- the whole directory was missing, so
             exchange-monitor.json and exchange-rates.json were never
             installed or distributed either.
       [x] 59.5 Shared gui helper lib/pn-currency-editors.[ch] (noinst, gui
             tier): the icon+ticker currency combo and the read-only monospace
             row, lifted out of pn-rate-gui.c rather than copied. pn-rate-gui.c
             shrank from 417 to 90 lines; both nodes now use the same editors.
       [x] 59.6 Tests (tests/unit/test-pn-bridge-quote.c, 97 checks, headless).
             Bodies trimmed from real provider replies are fed straight to the
             PnHttp emit_message vfunc, so the quote arithmetic is checked
             against numbers the providers actually returned. Verified live:
             100M PLS -> 1.792 BNB on PulseLN; 5M PLS -> 0.0793 BNB on
             ChangeNOW (PulseLN ~13% better on this route).
       [x] 59.7 Docs: data/help/PnBridgeQuote.html, new bag members
             (data.amount/from/to/bridge/fee/min_amount/max_amount/deprecated)
