             strokes themselves is under test, which is the payoff for the
             core/painter seam 80.4(i) and 80.10(d) already demanded.

             (a) THE SEAM IS AN API, and it shipped with 80.24 as
                 exactly that signature, over a pn_figure_render() that
                 hands the painter the same list:
                     GPtrArray *pn_figure_render (PnFigure *self,
                                                  double x, double y,
                                                  double w, double h);
                     gchar     *pn_figure_dump   (PnFigure *self,
                                                  double x, double y,
                                                  double w, double h);
                 core tier, newly-allocated multi-line string, one line
                 per executed statement INCLUDING the state changes, so
                 the pen machine is observable and not merely implied.
                 It is not a test-only hack -- it is the debugging tool
                 and the D-Bus automation surface as well.
             (b) THE FORMAT, which is the test oracle and therefore has
                 to be dull and stable:

                     # view 0 0 100 100 scale 1.00 rect 0 0 100 100
                     color rgb(32,32,32)
                     width 2.00
                     line 20.00 20.00 80.00 80.00
                     fill rgb(128,128,128)
                     poly 50.00 48.00 42.00 36.00 58.00 36.00
                     nofill
                     text 20.00 26.00 centre middle "A"
                     # skip 12 non-finite

                 DEVICE coordinates at %.2f, so the 80.4 transform is
                 under test rather than trusted; the leading comment
                 carries the window and the scale so a transform test
                 asserts them in one line; colours through
                 pn_color_to_string() rather than a second formatter;
                 text as anchor + alignment words + the string, never a
                 glyph box, because core cannot measure glyphs (80.7f);
                 and a SKIPPED statement leaves a `# skip <line>
                 <reason>` marker so 80.10(b) is asserted by presence
                 instead of by absence.
             (c) PICK RECTS WHERE THE SCALE IS 1. `view 0,0,100,100`
                 into a 100x100 rect gives s = 1, no letterbox, and
                 Y = 100 - v, so every expected number is checkable in
                 the head. Save the awkward arithmetic for the one
                 letterbox test that exists to exercise it (the
                 280x173 case: s = 2.3333, oy = 16.5).
             (d) LOCALE. Every number in the dump goes through
                 g_ascii_formatd / g_ascii_dtostr, or a machine with a
                 comma decimal separator fails every test. Add the
                 obvious guard: one case that sets LC_NUMERIC to a
                 comma locale and re-dumps, skipped when that locale is
                 not installed.
             (e) WHAT THE CASES COVER, roughly in this order: each verb
                 once; y-up (user y = 0 lands at device y = h); the
                 letterbox scale and centring; reversed bounds flipping
                 an axis; a degenerate `view` skipped with the previous
                 window standing (80.4d); pen state persisting down the
                 program AND resetting between frames (dump twice, get
                 the same string); assignment lines and free-variable
                 zero-fill (80.2.12); continuation lines, comments, and
                 a `#` inside a string; input binding and latching via
                 pn_node_receive_message_on_input(), the idiom
                 test-pn-expression2.c already uses; the 80.8(e)
                 snapshot surviving a repaint (receive once, dump
                 twice); and the three error classes -- (a) unknown
                 verb, bad arity, unterminated string, a `%s` format
                 (80.7c), a bad colour or dash literal, each asserted
                 through the exact `error` property text with an EMPTY
                 dump; (b) a NaN coordinate leaving a skip marker, the
                 rest of the figure drawn, `error` empty and has-error
                 FALSE; (c) a vector argument setting the error and
                 emptying the dump.
             (f) PLUMBING: tests/unit/test-pn-figure.c, added to BOTH
                 check_PROGRAMS (~line 36) and its own
                 test_pn_figure_SOURCES line in tests/unit/Makefile.am;
                 TESTS = $(check_PROGRAMS) so ./run-unit-tests.sh picks
                 it up. Then `automake && ./config.status` again
                 (80.9b). Usual conventions: pntest.h harness, no
                 g_test_init, one binary for this node.
             (g) The pn-expr-bind extraction from 80.8(c) is NOT tested
                 here: its safety net is the existing Calculator and
                 Calculator 2 tests passing untouched, which is the
                 whole point of calling it a characterization test.
